CONVERSATION 1: 34, a year of trying, everything normal

Lead: Hi, I'm 34 and we've been trying for over a year. Every test is normal and they've told me it's unexplained infertility. I feel completely stuck.

Lead: I don't even know what to do next.

Sonia: Unexplained is a description of what the tests covered, not a description of you. It means the standard workup didn't find the answer, which isn't the same as there not being one.

What did the workup actually include?

Lead: Bloods, an HSG, and a semen analysis for my husband. All fine.

Sonia: That's the standard set, and it's mostly built to rule out the big structural and hormonal causes. It's very good at that and it isn't designed to look at much else.

Has anyone gone into how you've been physically over the last couple of years? Sleep, weight changes, illness, stress, anything that shifted.

Lead: No, never. And honestly that period has been rough. My mum was ill, I changed jobs, I've barely slept properly in two years.

Sonia: Thank you for telling me that. It's the part of the picture that usually never gets asked about, and it's rarely nothing.

I'm not going to tell you that's the answer, because I don't know that yet. I will tell you it hasn't been examined and it's workable.

Lead: What would you actually do differently?

Sonia: Look at all of it at once instead of one system at a time, work out what in your case is most likely to matter, and then stay with you while you change it. Information on its own hasn't been your problem.

Is having a baby one of the biggest priorities in your life at the moment?

Lead: It's the only thing I think about.

Sonia: Then let's do this properly. My team will take the full history on a call and say plainly whether this is something I can move for you.

One thing before you put the time aside: it's a paid coaching program, and how much depends on the level of support.

Lead: That's fine. I'd rather pay for something that's actually been looked at.

Sonia: Then book whichever time suits.

